WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
"Fast X" is jam-packed with big names,&nbsp;
but one of the biggest names in Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.820
is conspicuously absent, and fans of&nbsp;
the "Fast" family aren't feeling it.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.140
On February 10th, the first trailer for&nbsp;
the 10th "Fast &amp; Furious" franchise film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.160
"Fast X," hit the internet, sparking&nbsp;
plenty of excitement among the series'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.900
ever-growing fanbase. "Fast" movies are big&nbsp;
by their very nature, but there are a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.260
reasons to believe that "Fast X" will&nbsp;
be the franchise's biggest entry yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.520
including this first trailer's runtime clocking&nbsp;
in at roughly three-and-a-half minutes in total.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.800
Perhaps the clearest indicator of the considerable&nbsp;
scale of "Fast X" is its out of control budget.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.440
Midway through its production, news broke that&nbsp;
"Fast X" had already cost producers $340 million,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.420
beating out the budget of the previous&nbsp;
film by $140 million. One of the key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.764
contributors to this outsized amount of&nbsp;
money is its absolutely stacked cast.

00:00:49.764 --> 00:00:51.444
"Game recognizes game."

00:00:51.444 --> 00:00:54.660
Absent from that all-star cast,&nbsp;
however, is Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.500
whose character Luke Hobbs joined the&nbsp;
team in "Fast Five," before eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.220
separating from the mainline series&nbsp;
for spinoff "Fast &amp; Furious Presents:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.600
Hobbs &amp; Shaw." While Johnson's unique trajectory&nbsp;
through the franchise is well-documented,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.500
some fans are nevertheless noting his&nbsp;
absence from the first "Fast X" trailer.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.180
On YouTube, plenty of commenters responded to&nbsp;
the "Fast X" trailer with excitement about its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.380
expansive cast featuring nearly every big&nbsp;
name from the franchise's history. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:24.537
some users argued that only with the addition of&nbsp;
Johnson could its cast truly be comprehensive.

00:01:24.537 --> 00:01:27.282
"You will never be able to break my family."

00:01:27.282 --> 00:01:31.800
In a Reddit discussion thread about the trailer, a&nbsp;
few commenters also described Johnson's absence as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.120
a detriment to an otherwise promising preview&nbsp;
for the film. For instance, one user wrote,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.540
"This looks great but it's missing&nbsp;
something without Dwayne, IMO."

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.960
Another user then replied that&nbsp;
Johnson's Luke Hobbs seems to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.080
the only major character that's&nbsp;
not a part of the "Fast X" cast.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.520
Plenty of Twitter users are discussing the&nbsp;
lack of Johnson in "Fast X" as well. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.520
user with Johnson in their avatar,&nbsp;
for example, shared that they feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.960
the inclusion of Jason Statham's Deckard&nbsp;
Shaw makes Johnson's absence particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:03.120
unusual. Another user even argued that Hobbs&nbsp;
should appear in "Fast X" for plot reasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.900
given that he had a hand in killing&nbsp;
Jason Momoa's character Dante's father.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.520
By now, Johnson's reasons for exiting the&nbsp;
mainline "Fast" franchise are well-known among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.540
fans of the series. A July 2021 profile&nbsp;
of Johnson in the Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.800
for example, recounts how Vin Diesel claimed&nbsp;
the discord between the two actors resulted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.000
from his attempts at eliciting a stronger&nbsp;
performance from Johnson. He told the outlet,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.664
"I laughed and I laughed hard.&nbsp;
I think everyone had a laugh at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.664 --> 00:02:30.240
that. I wish them the best of luck&nbsp;
on 'Fast 10' and 'Fast 11' and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.360
rest of the 'Fast &amp; Furious' movies&nbsp;
they do that will be without me."

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.460
Then, as recently as November of 2021, Diesel&nbsp;
introduced a new complication to his feud with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.840
Johnson when he praised his former co-star&nbsp;
and encouraged him to join "Fast X" anew.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.740
In response, Johnson shared that he felt&nbsp;
manipulated, particularly by the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.520
that Diesel invoked both his children&nbsp;
and the memory of Paul Walker. Johnson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.120
also revealed that he had privately&nbsp;
communicated to Diesel his desire to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.380
separate himself from the "Fast" franchise&nbsp;
in no uncertain terms a few months prior.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.540
From the sound of it, then, Diesel agrees with&nbsp;
fans who have argued that "Fast X" is incomplete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:07.920
without Johnson. Meanwhile, Johnson appears to&nbsp;
remain committed to separating himself from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.960
"Fast" films and Diesel in particular&nbsp;
for as long as the series continues.

